      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-11-24_WidnesExaminer_art0010" n="art0010">
        <head>WIDNES AND WARRINGTON.</head>
        <p>WIDNES AND WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>MR. JOHN R. GOODWIN continues to make ADVANCES FRIVATELY to Tradesmen, Farmers, Working-men and all respectable Hcaseholders, en their own security. aiONEY TO INCREASE YOUR STOCK. MONEY TO FURNISH YOUR HOUSE. MONEY TO PAY RENT OR DEBTS. Without Bondsmen, without delay, without public enquiry, on your simple written prcraise to pay back.—Apply et VIC- TORIA CHAMBERS (foot of the Central Station), WIDNES, and in WARRINGTON at my Residence, 134, Orford-lane. any Evening from 6tl 7. Applications from RUNCORN and District generally receive precisely the same attention.</p>
        <p>AMANCIIESTER GENTLEMAN having a large amount of Uninvested CAPITAL at his command is prepared to ADVANCH same to responsible Persons in Sums of .£lO to £lOOO,</p>
        <p>On the Borrower's simple written promise to repay;' Without Sureties, Delay. Law Costs or Publicity. Also on Deeds, Life Policii-s, at. syer cent interest.</p>
        <p>The amount Borrowed can be repaid by easy Instalments or capital can remain so lomf, as the interest is paid. as this office is a bona-fide private concern and not connected with any Loan Office. It is requested that habitual borrowers will not apply. For full particulars apply personally or by letter to J. CAMPBELL, ESQ., MAN.:HESTER CHAMBERS. 46a, MARKET-sTREET. MANCHESTER.</p>
