      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-11-24_WidnesExaminer_art0020" n="art0020">
        <head>HERE IS WHAT WE GIVE TO READERS</head>
        <p>HERE IS WHAT WE GIVE TO READERS</p>
        <p>OF THIS PAPER.</p>
        <p>You are interested in money making and no such opportunity for saving money has ever been presented to women who use knitting and fancy wools as that made to the readers of this paper by the Providence Mills Spinning Company. They are willing to send you some beautiful samples of knitting, embroidery and fancy wools for home knitting which may be kept by you. Their object is to show you that for a,npearanc,., wear and price they cannot be surpassed. In these days of scarcity of cash it is interesting to know the way tc buy the necessities of life direct from the manufacturers and thereby save threepence or more in each shillings- worth. We confidently recommend you to write to-day for patterns which will be sent free of charge by sending a; post-card with your name and address upon it. Kindly note that letters should be carefully addressed— Providence Mills Spinning Co., C. Department, Bradford, Yorkshire. N.B.—lf you would like they will also send you samples of their special dress fabrics as well as particu- htrs of their wonderful underwear.</p>
