        <p>LADY KEANE has much pleasure in recommending " Homocea" as an invaluable remedy for Rheumatism, Cuts, Bruises, Piles, Sprains, &amp;c.; she thinks so highly of it that she would not be without it in the house, as it Las entirely cured her of Rheumatism and other ail- ments. _ _ _</p>
        <p>The Rev. J. WILLIAM S. BUTCHER, 35, Park Road, East, Birkenhead, writes :—" I have great pleasure in complying with your request and in putting in writing what I have already said by word of mouth. I was much inconvenienced by a very irritating species of eczema. Several remedies that I have tried failed to give me more than a very temporary relief. I finally tried Homocea,' with happiest results. The relief was almost instantaneous,and, what is more to the point, the soothing effect remained, and a complete cure resulted. —Yours truly, J. WILLIAM BUTCHER."</p>
        <p>" Hoylake. Dear Sirs,—l want to thank you for that wonderful preparation, ' Homocea,' which we use for about everything ; but lately my little girl had a bad ringworm en the head, and my doctor said her hair would have to be cut close. But I preferred using the Homocea,' and in fur days it was quite well, and the doctor said I ought to give you a testimonial,and I think too.—Yours truly, M. ALDRED." All wholesale houses stock HOMOCEA. It can be ob- tained from Chemists and others at is. 1.0. or 2s. 9.1. per box, or will be sent bv post for is. 3d. and 3s. from the wholesale agency, 27, Haniilton Square, Birken- head. Sold in the neighbourhood by J. R. YOUNG, SANKEY- STREET, WARRINGTON by the executors of the late ISAAC SPEAKMAN,;BranoE-sTREET PHARMACY, RUN- CORN ;J. H. WESTON, DEVONSHIRE BUILDING, RUN- CORN ;S. STRINGFELLOW, 1, COLLEGE-STREET. Sr. HELENS; and by E. BOOTH, 5, CHESTER BRIDGE, CREWE.</p>
