        <p>GEXTIZACT FROM LETTER OF WITNESS BEARER:— Mrs. M. A. Smith, Orphan Home tor Girls, Croydon. To Mr. Taos. HALL.—" DEAR Sat, —I am pleased to testify to the great benefit derived from the use of your LUNG RESTORER, which I have given to s weral children in my Home—in two cases particularly its effects were marvel' bus, having cured most obstinate Coughs. I shall be pleased to recommend it to all my frirrids." CAUTION.—When you ask, ask for a Bottle of HALL'S LUNG RESTORER, don't be persuaded to accept anything else. Upon the oßtside wraprier of every genuine Bottle appears my Trade Mark (the figure of HOPE) and Signature. Beware of fraudulent imitations and innovations. Sold by Chemists and Stores everywhere; In Bottles, le. Ed. and 2s. 9d. Should there be aay difficulty in obtaining, it will be sent carriage paid, on receipt of P. 0.0. for the amount, from THOS. HALL, 24, Qut:ea Victoria- strect, tondo:, E,C.</p>
