        <p>CONSIDERATION.</p>
        <p>SIR.—My wife desires me to say that your Tudor Williams Balsam of Honey Is s prwed a most valuable medicine in ctur large family (eigist, children). As soon as Ett cough or a dold makes its appeirance a dose of Tudor's Balsam is at once administered, and his treatment is followed up until the cold disappears. Before using the Balsam in our family the children have been prostrate with colds for several weeks, but now, by taking doses, as directed they seem to suffer very little inconvenience. During the short time the cold is upon them the action of the Balsa-a is marvellous, and the little ones take it readily and ask for more. WALTER J. BRETT, C. 111., Headmaster Severn Tunnel School.</p>
        <p>March 16th, 1692.</p>
