      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-11-24_WidnesExaminer_art0112" n="art0112">
        <head>LANCASHIRE &amp; CHESHIRE COUNTY NEWSPAPERS</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE &amp; CHESHIRE COUNTY NEWSPAPERS</p>
        <p>WHICH COMPRISE rr HE Warrington # Mid-Cheshire Examiner, pub- lished Saturday morning. The district covered by the Paper comprises many populous rnaaufacturing towns and villages, and a large agricultural tract. THE Earlestown and Newton Examiner, and Ashton, Goiborne, and Haydock Reporter, published Friday afternoon. The district is in the heart of the Lancashire coal field.</p>
        <p>THE St. Helens Examtner and Preseot Weekly News, published Friday afternoon. The district comprises the centre of the Glass, Chemical, and Watch Trades of the King- cm, &amp;c.</p>
        <p>THE .Runcorn Examiner, published Friday after- noon. It is the only Weekly Paper in the district. and *Hers the best and cheapest facilities to advertisers. THE Widnes Examiner, published Friday after- noon. Widnes contains the largest number of Chemical Works of any town in the kingdom, and is rapidly becoming an important centre of industry.</p>
        <p>Auction, Education, Wanted, To be Let, On Sale, Legal Public Meeting, Sermon, Lecture, Bazaar, and other Public Notices, Advertisements (exceptParliamentary)are inserted in all the above papers at one charge.</p>
        <p>Each of the above papers consists of 8 pages. 56 long and wide columns,each column admitting more matter than the columns of any otherlocal paper—a fact deserving the attest tiers of both advertisers and subscribers. Each Erannner, in sddition to giving the local intelligence of the district. in which it circulates, contains the general news of the week.</p>
        <p>Price of each Paper—ONE PENNY.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-11-24_WidnesExaminer_art0113" n="art0113">
        <head>PREPAID ADVERTISEMENTS.</head>
        <p>PREPAID ADVERTISEMENTS.</p>
        <p>One Charge secures Insertion of the undermentioned Adver- tisements in ALL the FIVE EXAMINERS. WANTEDS, TO BE LETS, 18 WORDS, 6D.. ON SALES, } And 3d. for each succeeding 9 words.</p>
