        <p>NOTICE OF PARISH MEETING. PARISH OF LATCHFORD WITHOUT. 1. NOTICE is HEREBY GIVEN that the first Parish Meeting for the above names]. Parish will be held at the School Room of the Baptist Chapel in Wash- lane, on TUESDAY, the fourth day of December, 1894, at six o'clock in the evening. 2. The business to be transacted at the Meeting will be as follows:— (a) To elect a chairman for the Meeting. (b) To elect Parish Councillors. 3. The number of Parish Councillors to be elected at the meeting is eight. 4. Bach candidate for election as a Parish Councillor must be nominated in writing, and the nomination paper must be handed in at the Parish Meeting. 5. A parochial elector may sign eight nomination papers. but no more. S. Forms of nomination paper may be obtained, free of charge, from us at the Overseer's Office, Town Hall, Warring- ton. Dated this 22nd day of November, 1894. JOHN LUNT JAMES STRANGE lOverseers.</p>
        <p>NOTICE OF PARISH MEETING. PARISH OF LITTLE SANKEY. 1. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the first Parish Meeting for the above-named Parish will be held at the Wesleyan Schoolroom, Liverpool-road on TUBSDAY, the fourth day of December. 1894, at eight o'clock in the evening. 2. The business to be transacted at the Meeting will be as follows : (al To elect a Chairman for the Meeting. (b) To elect Parish Councillors. 3. The number of Parish Councillors to be elected at the Meeting is Seven. 4. Bach Candidate for election as a Parish Councillor must be nominated in writing and the nomination paper must be handed in at the Parish Meeting. 5. A parochial elector may sign seven nomination papers. but iso more. 8. Forms of nomination paper ,may be obtained, free of charge, from us at the Overseer's Office. Town Hall. War rington, or at the Office of Mr, J. C. Sutton, Bewsey-street, Warrington. Dated this 22nd clay of November, 1894. JOHN HARRISON, DANIEL JONES, THOMAS BIRTLES, Overseers. PETER LEIGH.</p>
