        <p>A NEW DEPARTUI:E IN THE FURNISHING g RADE. The extensive alterations necessitated by continued increase of business at the Manchester Louvre having now been almost completed, the Proprietors have pleasure in informing their old-establisfied "clientele" and the public generally, that the increased Exhibition Space in their Show-rooms (opposite All Saints' Church) has enabled th-m to stock and display an enormously added Quantity of FURNITURE—both New and Second-hand—so that their Customers have now a Collection to choose from which it's not too much to say is second to none in the United Kingdom. The recent extensive Sales held by us in consequence of Extension of Premises met with such a ready response from wide-awake clients, that our former Stock was speedily reduced and it became a serious question with us how to cope with the demands of fresh Customers. Whilst, of course the market is being flooded with New Modern Furniture, there scarcely ever was a time when High-class, Second-hand, Durable and Handsome SUITES were more difficult to obtain. But, ever on the alert, and first in the field, we are glad to say that we have been successful in securing one of the rarest and cotnpletest Collections of every variety of Furniture everoffered to the public since we entered the Trade. £lO,OOO OF NEWLY ADDED STOCK Now on offer at nearly one half of its original value. Railway Fares Paid to Country Customers. Catalogues Free on Appli- cation. THOSE ABOUTITO MARRY and those who contemplate adding to their present Stock of Furniture are specially invited to pay an early visit to the Manchester Louvre (opposite All Saints' Church). No one will be pressed ta buy, and our Salesmen have instructions to show the puhie through our Spacious and Elegant Show- rooms without importunity, as we rely upon the Furniture to recommend itself without puffing. The Extraordinary Stock which we now hold must be reduced without delay, as the prices paid by us will not allow for loss of interest on - accumulated quantities. Quick turnovers and small ,one suit our ch.4s of business. It will thus be seen what an immense advantage we are able to show over Rouses who hold their Stocks for months and months, and are obliged to charge the Public with the interest they lose on their sunk capital. Every facility is offered to intending purchasers. All goods are delivered free in our own carts and vans, or securely packed for transit by Rail, Carriage Paid. Every article is tested before hewing the premises, and, if necessary, skilled workmen will be sent out to plan carpets and fit the house up. Estimates given for the com- plete furnishing of a House from £2O te £l,OOO in value. Ad- vice gratis on the choice and selection of EVERY REQUISITE FOR COTTAGE OR MANSION. Parties visiting the Manchester Louvre should enter the Oxford-street, Rusholme, or Withington car at Piccadilly, and ask the conductor to stop at the MANCHESTER LOUVRE, where they will be est mished to find such spacious and elegantly appointed Showrooms, surpassing anything outside of London. Do not forget, that we now hold THE MOST COMPLETE COLLECTION OF FURNITURE EVER OFFERED. AT ABOUT ONE-HALE' iTS ORIGINAL COST. Absolutely unapproachable for Elegance, Comfort, Durability, and Cheapness. THIS WEEK'S LIST OF BARGAINS. 6ft. Brown Oak Sideboard, with lofty plate-glass back superbly carved ; original cost £75, price, £35, Solid Walnut Bedroom Suite, by Neild. cemprising sft fully enclosed wardrobe, pair of large-sized toilet tables with side reflecting mirrors, bedside pedestal, three chairs, and towel airer, price delivered. £23105., cheap. Bedroom Suite in satin walnut and Ash; 41t. wardrobe with bevelled glass door, pair of enclosed toilet tables, pedes. I Sal, three cane chairs and towel hirer, complete for £l2 125., worth £2O. Solid Walnut Suite, smaller size than above, with the same quantity of articles, 10 guineas. Breakfast Room Suite. all complete, £3 174 6d. Sideboard, in mahogany