        <p>Valuable Farms, Fields, Houses, Building Land, Ground Rents, Beerhouse. Shop, and other Properties in WARRINGTON, WOOLSTON, ORFORD, BURTON- WOOD, STOCKTON HEATH. APPLETON, STIiETTON. and LATCHFORD ; also Warrington Corporation Gas and Water Annuities, and Parr's Bank Shares. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION By Mr. JOHN MAINWARING. At the Hon Hotel, Warrington. on Wednesday, sth December, 1894, at 3 o'clock p.m. precisely, in the following lots or such other lots as may be determined at the time of sale, and subject to the Public Sale Conditions of the Incor- porated Law Society of Liverpool, and to special conditions to be then produced, and in the meantime to be obtained of the vendors' solicitors :- LOT 1.-A Freehold MEADOW FIELD, containing about 2a. 3r. 30p., in Arpley Meadows, Warrington (near Walton Arches), occupied by the late Mr. John Wainwright's Representatives. LOT 2.-A Freehold FIELD, in Stretton, containing about 5a lr. 12p., having a good frontage to the highroad fsom Warrington to Whitley, in the occupation of Mr. Joseph Smith. L T 3.- A Freehold FARM, in Cross-lane. Appleton, with House and Outbuildings, in the occupation of Mr. John Dirchfield ; also a Freehold COTTAGE and GARDEN adjoin lug, in the occupation of Mr. Robert Roughsedge; contents" ' 24a. 3r. 21p. LOT 4.-Two Freehold DWELLING-HOUSES, with Gar- dens and Orchard. and several Fields. in Cross-lane, in Appleton. containing 16a. Or. 22p., in the occupation of Mr. Joseph Knowles, or his subtenant. Mr. Richard Holcroft,and of Mrs. James Knowles. or her subtenant. LOT 5. A Freehold COTTAGE and GARDEN in Cross- lane, Appleton, in the occupation of Mr. Thomas Bate, con- taining about 21 perches. LOT 6.-A Freehold DWELLING-HOUSE, known as! " Whitefield," with Gardens, lately in the occupation of Mr. George Hatton (deceased), in Red-lane, Appleton ; also a Freehold COI TAGR adjoining, in the occupation of Mr. John Shaw. There will also be included in this lot a Piece of Lead at the back, forming portion of a field, in the occupation of Mr. John Weir. This will make the lot an excellent and valu- able building site, with a frontage of about 208 feet to Red- lane, the whole containing about 3,484 square yards. LOT 7.-A Freehold Plot of valuable BUILDING LAND, in Red-lane, Appleton, adjoining Lot 6, and having a frontage of about 210 feet to Red-lane, and containing about 3,201 square yards, with two Cottages thereon, in the several occu- pations of Mr. John Shaw, Mr. Philip Howell, Miss A. B. Gill, and Mr. John Weir. LOT 8.-A Freehold Plot of valuable BUILDING LAND in Red-lane. Appleton, adjoining Lot 7, and having a frontage of about 200 feet to Red-lane, and containing about 4.049 square yards, in the several occupations of Mr. John Hedg- ccck. Miss Gill, and Mr. John Weir. LOT 9 -A Freehold Plot of valuable BUILDING LAND in Red-lane. Appletan, adjoining Lot 6, and having a frontage of abo a 200 feet to Red-lane, an I containing about 3,555 square yards, in the occupation of Mr. John Weir. LOT 10.-Valuable Freehold BUILDING LAND in and near Red-lane, Appl, ton. in the occupation of Mr. John Weir, containing about Ba. lr. 7lp. This lot is admirably suited for development for building purposes. LOT 11.-A valuable Plot of BUILDING LAND in Red- lane, Appleton, in the oecupation of Mr. Thomas Hampson, containing about 3,105 square yards. This is an excellent building site. It is sold,subject to this covenants entered into by the late Mr. George Hatton with the Bridgewater Trastees, which are specified in the special conditions of sale. LOT 12.-Two Freehold FIELDS in Woelston, having along frontage to the highway from Warrington to Manehester. containing about 19a. Or. 25p., in the occupation of Mr. Thomas Houghton. This lot is very suitable for building land. LOT 13.-A Freehold FARM, called Brookhouse Farm, in Long-lane, Orford. in the occupation of Mr. John Hankey, consisting of a farmhouse and outbuildings and three fields in a ring fence containing about 14a. 